      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "dae9e379-53fe-57ec-87c6-8824bc35e772",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charlie Walker, George D. Hay\n- Organizations: Grand Ole Opry, Country Radio DJ Hall of Fame, WSM\n- Places: Copeville, Texas, Nashville, Tennessee\n- Products: \"Little Old Wine Drinker Me\", \"Wine, Woman & Walker\"\n- Topics: Country music\n\nFacts:\n- George D. Hay founded the Grand Ole Opry on November 28, 1925, as a one-hour radio \"barn dance\" on WSM in Nashville, Tennessee.\n- Charlie Walker was born on November 2, 1926, in Copeville, Texas, and became an American country musician.\n- Charlie Walker first released the song \"Little Old Wine Drinker Me\" in 1966 on the album \"Wine, Woman & Walker\".\n- Charlie Walker held membership in the Grand Ole Opry from 1967.\n- Charlie Walker was inducted into the Country Radio DJ Hall of Fame in 1981.\n- Charlie Walker died on September 12, 2008.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
